    {
      "code": "PARTLY_CALLABLE_BINS",
      "severity": "info",
      "message": "This input records which bins are called (at least 10% of their 100 bases callable, fq2psmcfa's rule) but not how many of their bases are, as psmcfa does, so the fit treats every called bin as 100 bases, as C psmc does. 18.6% of bins are missing (N), and 1,901,098 called bins (8.1% of them) border those runs: they hold fewer than 100 callable bases unless a run starts or ends at a bin boundary. If missing data are also scattered in runs shorter than a bin, most called bins do, which this input cannot show. Partly callable bins show fewer heterozygous sites, which biases theta, the times and Ne low by about their missing share.",
      "recommendation": "To measure it, run `psmc-rs qc` on the data the psmcfa was made from: a VCF with its callable mask (--vcf-mask) or an all-sites VCF from `bcftools call -c`. It reports the share of callable bases of the called bins, and a fit of that VCF weighs each bin by its callable bases (--bin-callable auto), which removes the bias.",
      "sequences": []
    }
  ],
